Idea (Level Order Traversal):
Perform Level Order Traversal (BFS).
At each level, print the first node.
Alternative approach:
Use recursion and track the maximum level visited.
Steps (BFS Method):
Use a queue.
Insert root node.
For each level:
Get number of nodes at that level.
Print the first node.
Add left and right children.
Repeat until queue is empty.
